---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Interactive Essay Lab Kit — Julian Codespoti"
  description="The reusable Astro + MDX + React simulation framework powering interactive technical articles on this site."
  activeNav="framework"
>
  <main class="page-shell">
    <div class="hero-eyebrow">
      <span class="hero-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span>Reusable authoring kit · src/kit/</span>
    </div>

    <h1 class="home-title">How these interactive articles are built.</h1>
    <p class="home-lead">
      Writing an interactive systems article should feel like writing Markdown with drop-in live laboratories—never
      rebuilding scroll spies, dark/light themes, offscreen animation pausing, or accessible controls from scratch.
    </p>

    <div class="stat-grid" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-label">Prose JS overhead</div>
        <div class="stat-value" style="color: var(--emerald);">0 KB</div>
        <div class="stat-sub">Static HTML via Astro + Shiki; islands hydrate on viewport entry.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-label">Offscreen CPU</div>
        <div class="stat-value" style="color: var(--cyan);">Paused</div>
        <div class="stat-sub">Shared <code>useStageVisibility()</code> halts rAF loops automatically.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-label">Authoring format</div>
        <div class="stat-value" style="color: var(--accent-strong);">MDX</div>
        <div class="stat-sub">Drop a new <code>.mdx</code> in <code>src/content/essays/</code> and push.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="essay-prose">
      <h2>Reusable primitives in <code>src/kit/</code></h2>
      <ul>
        <li><code>&lt;LabStage&gt;</code> — Full-bleed framed laboratory container with kicker badge, live telemetry <code>&lt;MetricPill&gt;</code> bar, dot-grid simulation stage, bottom control bar, and semantic caption.</li>
        <li><code>&lt;Slider&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;Segmented&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;Toggle&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;ActionButton&gt;</code> — Keyboard-accessible, tabular-num controls styled consistently across dark and warm-paper light themes.</li>
        <li><code>&lt;Scrubber&gt;</code> — Multi-step walkthrough controller with Play/Pause auto-advance, Prev/Next stepping, and synchronized step cards.</li>
        <li><code>useStageVisibility()</code> — Shared React hook wiring <code>IntersectionObserver</code> + <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> so 60fps canvas labs never burn battery offscreen.</li>
        <li><code>&lt;Callout&gt;</code> &amp; <code>&lt;StatGrid&gt;</code> — Editorial callouts and measured benchmark grids that break out cleanly beyond the 68ch reading measure.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Adding a new interactive article</h2>
      <p>Create <code>src/content/essays/my-topic.mdx</code> with frontmatter, build your simulation islands under <code>src/sims/my-topic/</code>, and mount them with <code>client:visible</code>:</p>

      <pre><code>{`---
title: "My Interactive Systems Post"
subtitle: "Why the obvious implementation breaks under real load."
description: "An interactive walkthrough..."
pubDate: 2026-12-01
readingTime: "10 min read"
simsCount: 3
tags: ["Rust", "Networking"]
---
import { MyLab } from "../../sims/my-topic/MyLab";

Here is what happens when packets back up:

<MyLab client:visible />`}</code></pre>

      <p>
        Push to <code>main</code> and GitHub Actions builds and publishes the static bundle straight to GitHub Pages.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
